1
00:05:16,153 --> 00:05:22,153
They say money makes the world go round. But sex was invented before money.

2
00:10:32,307 --> 00:10:38,307
The Two Jakes is a crime, drama, mystery film directed by Jack Nicholson.

3
00:15:48,461 --> 00:15:54,461
Real estate developer Jake Berman hires private investigator and war
veteran Jake Gittes for some run-of-the-mill matrimonial work.

4
00:21:04,615 --> 00:21:10,615
After Berman shoots his wife's lover, who happens to be his business partner, Gittes is drawn
into a web of conspiracy and deceit involving the oil reserves beneath Los Angeles.

5
00:26:20,769 --> 00:26:26,769
While investigating, Gittes hears a voice from his past that
causes him to revisit a traumatic case in Chinatown.

6
00:31:36,923 --> 00:31:42,923
J.J. "Jake" Gittes, played by Jack Nicholson.

7
00:36:53,076 --> 00:36:59,076
Julius "Jake" Berman, played by Harvey Keitel.

8
00:42:09,230 --> 00:42:15,230
Kitty Berman, played by Meg Tilly.

9
00:47:25,384 --> 00:47:31,384
Lillian Bodine, played by Madeleine Stowe.

10
00:52:41,538 --> 00:52:47,538
Cotton Weinberger, played by Eli Wallach.

11
00:57:57,692 --> 00:58:03,692
Mickey Nice, played by Rubén Blades.

12
01:03:13,846 --> 01:03:19,846
The Two Jakes is a 1990 American neo-noir mystery film
and the sequel to the 1974 film Chinatown.

13
01:08:30,000 --> 01:08:36,000
Directed by and starring Jack Nicholson, who reprises his role of J.J.

14
01:13:46,153 --> 01:13:52,153
“Jake” Gittes from the first film, the cast also features Harvey Keitel, Meg Tilly, Madeleine Stowe,
Richard Farnsworth, Frederic Forrest, David Keith, Rubén Blades, Tracey Walter and Eli Wallach.

15
01:19:02,307 --> 01:19:08,307
Also reprising their roles from Chinatown are Joe Mantell, Perry Lopez,
James Hong, and, in a brief voice-over, Faye Dunaway.

16
01:24:18,461 --> 01:24:24,461
The musical score for the film is by Van Dyke Parks, who
also appears as a prosecuting attorney.

17
01:29:34,615 --> 01:29:40,615
Set a decade after the first film, The Two Jakes follows private investigator Gittes as he becomes
embroiled in a web of corruption, adultery, and murder involving a client, also named Jake.

18
01:34:50,769 --> 01:34:56,769
The deeper he goes, the more he realizes the events may be related to
the events surrounding Evelyn Mulwray ten years prior.

19
01:40:06,923 --> 01:40:12,923
The Two Jakes faced a troubled production and went
through several years of development hell.

20
01:45:23,076 --> 01:45:29,076
Various actors were attached at several points, including Joe Pesci and Roy Scheider, with screenwriter
Robert Towne also at one point set to direct and producer Robert Evans set to co-star.

21
01:50:39,230 --> 01:50:45,230
Filming finally took place with Nicholson at the helm, filming
around Los Angeles in the early summer of 1989.

22
01:55:55,384 --> 01:56:01,384
The film was released by Paramount Pictures on August 10, 1990.

23
02:01:11,538 --> 02:01:17,538
It received mixed reviews and was not a box office success, and plans for a
third film, with Gittes near the end of his life, were abandoned.

24
02:06:27,692 --> 02:06:33,692
The film explores themes of los angeles,
california, private detective, neo-noir.

25
02:11:43,846 --> 02:11:49,846
The tone is mind_bending and dark and emotional.
